# 🧠 PART 2 — DSA MASTER REVISION

## Your pattern recognition cheat sheet

| If the problem says...              | Think...                |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| Fast lookup                         | HashMap / Set           |
| Sorted + pair                       | Two Pointers            |
| Contiguous + longest/shortest       | Sliding Window          |
| Range sum                           | Prefix Sum              |
| Sorted search                       | Binary Search           |
| Minimum feasible answer             | Binary Search on Answer |
| Next greater/smaller                | Monotonic Stack         |
| Kth / Top K                         | Heap                    |
| Take / Don't Take                   | DP                      |
| Generate all possibilities          | Backtracking            |
| Tree traversal                      | DFS / BFS               |
| Unweighted shortest path            | BFS                     |
| Weighted non-negative shortest path | Dijkstra                |
| Dependencies                        | Topological Sort        |
| Connectivity                        | DFS/BFS/DSU             |
| Minimum spanning tree               | Kruskal / Prim          |

### 🔥 Your new rule:

> **Don't ask “Which problem is this?” Ask “What structure does this problem have?”**

