# ⚙️ PART 6 — OS FINAL MASTER REVISION

## Process vs Thread

```text
Process
→ Independent execution unit
→ Own address space

Thread
→ Execution unit inside a process
→ Threads share process resources
```

## CPU Scheduling

Know:

```text
FCFS
SJF
SRTF
Priority
Round Robin
```

### Round Robin

Uses:

> **Time Quantum**

---

# 💀 DEADLOCK

Four necessary conditions:

```text
Mutual Exclusion
Hold and Wait
No Preemption
Circular Wait
```

Memory:

# **MHNC**

---

# 🧠 MEMORY MANAGEMENT

Know the difference:

```text
Paging
→ Fixed-size pages/frames

Segmentation
→ Logical variable-sized segments
```

### Virtual Memory

Allows processes to use an address space larger than available physical memory by moving data between memory and secondary storage.

